                    91.0,
                    1255.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Table I summarizes the modeling-level distinction between RadioTrace and representative prior-based inverse RM estimation methods. Existing methods mainly operate at the RM level by updating reconstructed RM estimates or posterior RM samples, whereas RadioTrace refines the Tx locations that condition subsequent RM generation.",
